{
  "setup": "Three synchronized 16-kHz physical close microphones and earlier three labeled solo pilots, one speaker at a time with all mics recording. The output is the fixed standard waveform multiplied by a bounded time-varying gain. No reordering. Frozen filter has 1.024 s centered speech hold and limits reduction to 6.02 dB. The method cannot consume a single mixed microphone for these scores.",
  "chronology": "The M8014 early development panel selected the preliminary presence threshold. The original 244 fixtures form a secondary reused comparison. M8006/M8007 showed a regression under a predecessor. A sustained hold and gentler amplitude floor were fixed before all M8009 comparisons. Donors in every evaluated case occur after the first 45% cut and are disjoint from calibration. The lower-count companions remove one or two source images from each original trial and use the same donors, so they are paired controls. The 17 M8009 clips come from a new group of three original speakers in a previously studied physical room.",
  "metric": "All three fixed targets must pass alignment and the existing speech-retention criterion. In constructed one/two talker controls, evaluate mean-square absent-microphone output in intervals where all selected talkers are active; positive dB means less output. Levels include captured room noise. Each inactive receiver is a separate observation. An energy drop does not prove improved intelligibility.",
